@vsm 1.0
// SEED only — full spec.vsm to be written when EXP-PHI-02 is scheduled
// domain_context: {target=claude-qwen-s1, env=VSF-session, layer=S2/S3↔S1}
// origin: H6 (operational_fidelity) emerged in EXP-PHI-01 Run 005
// principle source: dynamics_choice.vsm §paper2_implications + Qwen R1 split-operator analogy

experiment_seed(phi_loop_v2, "computed vs interpreted brief fields — S2-parser delegation"):

  motivation:
    "EXP-PHI-01 Run 005 closed the loop but with 60% fidelity (3/5 keys correct).
     Counting bias in qwen2.5-coder:7b under-estimated s_level_mentions by ~5×.
     The fix is NOT to teach the LLM to count — it is to NOT ask the LLM to count.

     Cibernetic principle: variety belongs to the layer competent to handle it.
     Computation = deterministic variety → S2 (parser, cgroup of computation).
     Interpretation = semantic variety → S1 (LLM execution).

     This experiment formalizes the split in the VSL brief grammar itself."

  hypotheses:
    H7_split_fidelity:
      "If brief.output_format is partitioned into:
         computed: {key: parseable_pattern}
         interpreted: {key: semantic_description}
       and wrapper executes each by appropriate layer,
       then:
         P(correct | computed_field) = 1 (deterministic)
         P(correct | interpreted_field) = capability-dependent
       and total fidelity = weighted average, separable per axis."

    H8_compression_via_split:
      "When LLM only handles interpreted_fields, prompt is shorter
       (no need to inline full file content for counting tasks).
       Predicted: brief_bytes_v2 < brief_bytes_v1 / 2 (filtered input)
       Predicted: latency_e2e_v2 < latency_e2e_v1 / 3 (less prompt + less generation)"

    H9_capability_taxonomy:
      "Cataloging which fields are 'reliably computable' vs 'reliably interpretable'
       per LLM model size yields a capability matrix.
       Hypothesis: the boundary between computed/interpreted is model-specific
       and quantifiable as a fidelity-per-task profile."

  proposed_brief_grammar:
    output_format: {
      computed: {
        // wrapper-executed via deterministic parser
        // ground_truth.json comparison expected to be 100%
        line_count: "INTEGER",
        token_frequencies: "OBJECT<string, INTEGER>",
        regex_matches: "ARRAY<{pattern: STRING, count: INTEGER}>",
      },
      interpreted: {
        // LLM-executed via semantic reasoning
        // ground_truth optional (may have multiple valid answers)
        summary: "STRING ≤ 200 words",
        key_themes: "ARRAY<STRING> ≤ 5 elements",
        cybersyn_mapping: "OBJECT<term, S_level>",
      },
    }

  proposed_protocol:
    n_runs: 5  // for H7 reproducibility
    substrate: "Ollama qwen2.5-coder:7b on LXC 101 (post-EXP-PHI-01-warmup)"
    wrapper: "scripts/run_phi02_split.py — extends run_phi01_ollama.py with parser layer"
    metrics: [
      "fidelity_computed: {key: bool} — should be 1.0 always",
      "fidelity_interpreted: {key: human-rated 0-1} — variable",
      "latency_e2e", "brief_bytes", "result_bytes (split)",
      "comparison vs PHI-01 baseline: latency reduction, prompt reduction",
    ]

  unblocks_for_paper2:
    "§3 fidelity vs viability: H7 demonstrates separability empirically
     §4 capability-aware briefs: H9 produces first capability matrix
     methodological: parser-delegation pattern as VSL grammar v2.0 standard"

  prereq:
    - "task(T) VSL parser ~200 líneas Python — REQUIRED before this experiment"
    - "EXP-PHI-01 done — DONE 2026-05-09"

  status: "SEED — full spec to write when scheduled (after task T closes)"

⟦ /phi_loop_v2_seed | EXP-PHI-02 | vsm-1.0 | 2026-05-09 ⟧
